{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Beth Robinson (born March 6, 1965) is an American lawyer and judge from Vermont who serves on the Vermont Supreme Court.","title":"Beth Robinson"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Her nomination, made by Governor Peter Shumlin in October 2011, was confirmed by a unanimous vote of the Vermont Senate on February 7, 2012.","title":"Beth Robinson"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2014 Vermont gubernatorial election took place on November 4, 2014, to elect the Governor of Vermont, concurrently with elections to the United States Senate in other states and elections to the United States House of Representatives and various state and local elections.","title":"Vermont gubernatorial election, 2014"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Incumbent Democratic Governor Peter Shumlin ran for re-election to a third term in office against Republican businessman Scott Milne, Libertarian businessman Dan Feliciano and several other minor party and independent candidates.","title":"Vermont gubernatorial election, 2014"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Point ("Independent Radio, The Point") is a radio network operating in the state of Vermont.","title":"The Point (radio network)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The station first signed on as a single frequency local Montpelier station (WNCS) in 1977.","title":"The Point (radio network)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was started by Jeb Spaulding who is the current Chancellor of the Vermont State Colleges and former State Treasurer of Vermont and Secretary of Administration under Vermont Governor Peter Shumlin.","title":"The Point (radio network)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Although at that time there was no designated Adult Album Alternative format, The Point's programming format has been solidly Adult Album Alternative/Progressive for its entire history.","title":"The Point (radio network)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Helen Riehle is an American politician from the state of Vermont who served as a U.S. Republican Party member of the Vermont Senate, representing all of Chittenden County except for the town of Colchester.","title":"Helen Riehle"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is chair of the South Burlington City Council and resides in that city.","title":"Helen Riehle"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Having previously served in both the State House and Senate, she was appointed by Governor Peter Shumlin in March 2016 to succeed Diane Snelling, who had earlier resigned.","title":"Helen Riehle"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"George B. "Jeb" Spaulding (born December 28, 1952 in Manchester, Massachusetts) is the current chancellor of the Vermont State Colleges.","title":"Jeb Spaulding"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He previously served as Vermont State Treasurer and as Governor Peter Shumlin's secretary of administration.","title":"Jeb Spaulding"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Deborah "Deb" Markowitz is a Visiting Professor of Environmental Policy and Leadership at the University of Vermont Rubenstein School of Environment and Natural Resources.","title":"Deborah Markowitz"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She served from 2011-2017 as the Secretary of the Vermont Agency of Natural Resources.","title":"Deborah Markowitz"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She was appointed by Vermont Governor Peter Shumlin.","title":"Deborah Markowitz"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Prior to this, Markowitz was elected six times to serve as the Secretary of State of Vermont.","title":"Deborah Markowitz"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Although she is a member of the Democratic Party, she won the nomination of both the Republican and Democratic Parties in two of her races.","title":"Deborah Markowitz"}],"peer_messages":["title":"The Point (radio network)"}
